WEBVTT

00:00.330 --> 00:02.965
- [Voiceover] Chepi is an
ecologist who studies the change

00:02.965 --> 00:06.784
in the narwhal population of
the Arctic ocean over time.

00:06.784 --> 00:10.720
She observed that the
population population loses 5.6%

00:10.720 --> 00:14.144
of its size every 2.8 months.

00:14.144 --> 00:16.129
The population of narwhals can be modeled

00:16.129 --> 00:18.602
by a function, N, which
depends on the amount

00:18.602 --> 00:20.533
of time, t in months.

00:20.533 --> 00:22.889
When Chepi began the study, she observed

00:22.889 --> 00:27.765
that there were 89,000
narwhals in the Arctic ocean.

00:27.765 --> 00:30.771
Write a function that models
the population of narwhals

00:30.771 --> 00:33.898
t months since the
beginning of Chepi's study.

00:33.898 --> 00:35.175
Like always, pause the video

00:35.175 --> 00:36.312
and see if you can do it on your own

00:36.312 --> 00:38.530
before we work through it together.

00:38.530 --> 00:39.930
So let's now work through it together.

00:39.930 --> 00:42.032
To get my essence of what
this function is to do,

00:42.032 --> 00:45.711
it's always valuable to
see, to create a table

00:45.711 --> 00:48.033
for some interesting
inputs for the function

00:48.033 --> 00:52.131
and seeing how the function should behave.

00:52.131 --> 00:53.914
So first of all, if t is in months

00:53.914 --> 00:57.815
and N of t is, in N is the,

00:57.815 --> 01:01.878
that models, N is the number
of narwhals, the narwhals.

01:01.878 --> 01:04.200
So what, when T is equal to zero,

01:04.200 --> 01:05.593
what is N of zero?

01:05.593 --> 01:07.357
Well, we know a T equals zero.

01:07.357 --> 01:10.503
There are 89,000 narwhals in the ocean.

01:10.503 --> 01:13.882
So 89,000.

01:13.882 --> 01:16.819
And now, what's another interesting one?

01:16.819 --> 01:17.674
Well, T is in months

01:17.674 --> 01:19.822
and we know that the population decreases

01:19.822 --> 01:22.840
5.6% every 2.8 months.

01:22.840 --> 01:26.044
So let's think about when T is 2.8,

01:26.044 --> 01:27.425
2.8 months.

01:27.425 --> 01:28.900
Well then the population,

01:28.900 --> 01:32.847
it should have gone down 5.6%.

01:32.847 --> 01:36.179
So going down 5.6% is the same thing

01:36.179 --> 01:37.839
as retaining.

01:37.839 --> 01:40.799
What's one minus 5.6%?

01:40.799 --> 01:45.106
Retaining 94.4%.

01:45.106 --> 01:45.744
I'll be clear.

01:45.744 --> 01:47.908
100%,

01:47.908 --> 01:51.625
if you lose 5.6%,

01:51.625 --> 01:56.625
you are going to be left with 94.4%.

01:57.354 --> 01:59.606
The 0.6 plus 0.4 gets you a 95

01:59.606 --> 02:01.069
plus another five is 100.

02:01.069 --> 02:02.929
So another way of saying, this sentence,

02:02.929 --> 02:06.748
that the population loses 5.6%
of its size every 2.8 months

02:06.748 --> 02:09.465
is to say that the population is 94%,

02:09.465 --> 02:12.785
94.4% of its size every 2.8 months

02:12.785 --> 02:16.604
or shrinks to 94.4% of its original size

02:16.604 --> 02:19.669
every, or let me phrase this clearly.

02:19.669 --> 02:22.687
After every 2.8 months, the population,

02:22.687 --> 02:25.102
you can either say it shrinks 5.6%

02:25.102 --> 02:27.865
or you could say it has, it's gone from,

02:27.865 --> 02:31.348
it's 94.4% of the
population at the beginning

02:31.348 --> 02:32.902
of those 2.8 months.

02:32.902 --> 02:37.902
So after 2.8 months, the
population should be 89,000 times,

02:38.172 --> 02:40.413
I could write times 94.4%

02:40.413 --> 02:44.789
or I could write times 0.944.

02:44.789 --> 02:48.442
Now, if we go another 2.8 months,

02:48.442 --> 02:51.622
so two times 2.8.

02:51.622 --> 02:53.329
I have to say you could
just write that as,

02:53.329 --> 02:55.129
I could write that as 5.6 months

02:55.129 --> 02:56.951
but let me just write this is 2.8 months.

02:56.951 --> 02:57.706
Where are we gonna be?

02:57.706 --> 03:00.132
We're gonna be 89,000

03:00.132 --> 03:03.309
times 0.944.

03:03.309 --> 03:04.470
This is where we were before

03:04.470 --> 03:05.666
at the beginning of this period.

03:05.666 --> 03:08.046
Now, we're gonna be 94.4% of that.

03:08.046 --> 03:10.696
So we're gonna multiply by 94.4% again

03:10.696 --> 03:13.154
or 0.944 again

03:13.154 --> 03:16.868
or we can just say times 0.944 squared.

03:16.868 --> 03:20.998
And after three of these periods,

03:20.998 --> 03:24.235
well, we're gonna be times 0.944 again.

03:24.235 --> 03:26.812
So it's gonna be 89,000

03:26.812 --> 03:31.812
times 0.944 squared

03:32.133 --> 03:33.909
times 0.944

03:33.909 --> 03:37.171
which is gonna be 0.944
to the third power.

03:37.171 --> 03:39.331
And I think you might
see what's going on here.

03:39.331 --> 03:41.721
We have an exponential function.

03:41.721 --> 03:43.370
Between every 2.8 months,

03:43.370 --> 03:45.961
we are multiplying by this common ratio

03:45.961 --> 03:48.399
of 0.944.

03:48.399 --> 03:52.404
And so we could write our function N of t.

03:52.404 --> 03:57.311
Our initial value is 89,000

03:57.311 --> 04:02.261
times 0.944

04:02.261 --> 04:04.943
to the power of, however, many of these

04:04.943 --> 04:07.585
2.8 month period we've gone so far.

04:07.585 --> 04:09.396
So if we take the number of months

04:09.396 --> 04:11.567
and we divide by 2.8, that's how many

04:11.567 --> 04:14.446
2.8 month period we have gotten gone.

04:14.446 --> 04:16.815
And so notice, when t equals zero,

04:16.815 --> 04:18.115
all of this turns into one,

04:18.115 --> 04:19.752
erasing the zero part, that becomes one.

04:19.752 --> 04:21.029
You have 89,000.

04:21.029 --> 04:24.326
When t is equal to 2.8,
this exponent is one.

04:24.326 --> 04:27.448
Now we're gonna multiply by 0.944 once.

04:27.448 --> 04:30.908
When t is 5.6, the exponent
is going to be two.

04:30.908 --> 04:34.066
Now we're gonna multiply by 0.944 twice.

04:34.066 --> 04:36.285
And I'm just doing the values that make

04:36.285 --> 04:38.219
the exponent integers
but it's going to work

04:38.219 --> 04:39.346
for the ones in between.

04:39.346 --> 04:40.702
I encourage you to graph it

04:40.702 --> 04:43.581
or to try those values in
a calculator if you like.

04:43.581 --> 04:44.958
But there you have it, we're done.

04:44.958 --> 04:47.540
We have modeled our narwhals.

04:47.540 --> 04:50.553
So let me just underline
that and we're done.
